# L §8.2 (tally 2.3, #247; the review of G3, N6 (i)): a balance that is a hole because a calendar's hole dates a
# move (q4 in scenario sq, q13 under a pin of the calendar) lists no `held:` or `pinned:` line for the calendar's
# reads on other days: as the engine, the first pin's refcore and tally 2.2.1's. Before (W2's refcore, 9d09228a):
# a `pinned:` line and 34 `held:` lines; taken back with W1's two hole-day additions at 19763ae5.
=== scn.tally
model scn
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2028-12-31
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
source s "invented"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input pay: money PLN
input holidays: calendar
input hol2: calendar
input hol3: calendar
def pay_on[m in months]: date = schedule(m, n_5, following, holidays)
move salary[m in months]: transfers
  on pay_on[m]
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay
input n_5: int
input d_20270430: date
input d_20270405: date
input d_20260301: date
input d_20270406: date
input d_20270402: date
input n_1: int
version base
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  pay = 1000.00 PLN "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
version pins
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  hol2 = calendar(weekends [sat, sun, mon]) "c"
  hol3 = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], added [?"hol3 day?"]) "c"
version calv
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  holidays = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], yearly [01-01, 05-03, 12-25], added [2027-04-05]) "c"
version late
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-06-01
  replace holidays = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], yearly [01-01, 05-03, 12-25], added [2027-04-06]) "later"
version autov
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  n_5 = 5 "c"
  d_20270430 = 2027-04-30 "c"
  d_20270405 = 2027-04-05 "c"
  d_20260301 = 2026-03-01 "c"
  d_20270406 = 2027-04-06 "c"
  d_20270402 = 2027-04-02 "c"
  n_1 = 1 "c"
ask q4: bal(konto, d_20270430) in sq
ask q13: bal(konto, d_20270430) with holidays = hol3
=== sq.tally
scenario sq over scn
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01
version sqv
  cite s
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace holidays = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], yearly [01-01, 05-03, 12-25], added [?"which Monday of April 2027 is Spring Day?"]) "s"
=== expect q4 q13
q4: ?"which Monday of April 2027 is Spring Day?" (holidays)
  world: sq
  cut 2027-01-01
q13: ?"hol3 day?" (holidays)
  cut 2027-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input d_20260301 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input d_20270402 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input d_20270405 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input d_20270406 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input hol2 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input n_1 is read by nothing
